<title>BULGARIA: Yield down to 0.90 pct on Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield down to 0.90 pct on Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yield fell further on Bulgaria's Finance Ministry issue of 18 billion levs of four-week discount T-bills at the daily auction on Friday as the issue was heavily oversubscribed, central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>The average yield to maturity on the issue was 0.90 percent, down from 1.71 on Thursday and 2.57 percent on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3038597004</p>
<p> Maturity			four weeks</p>
<p> Par value		     18,000 million levs</p>
<p> Issue date		    June 16</p>
<p> Maturity date		 July 14</p>
<p> Bids received		 61,489.7 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   98.79 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		 18,000 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  99.11 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     0.90 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
